.TH "GF-REPORTS-SEND-REPORT" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-reports-send-report - Sends a report


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf reports send-report [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends a report

.PP
Generate and send a report. This API waits for the report to be generated before returning. We recommend that you set the client’s timeout to at least 60 seconds. Available to org admins only and with a valid license.

.PP
Only available in Grafana Enterprise v7.0+. This API endpoint is experimental and may be deprecated in a future release. On deprecation, a migration strategy will be provided and the endpoint will remain functional until the next major release of Grafana.

.PP
You need to have a permission with action \fBreports:send\fR\&.

.PP
Body schema (ReportEmail):
{
  "emails": string,
  "id": string,
  "useEmailsFromReport": boolean
}


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	The path to the body json file or json string. For example, --body=/path/to/body.json or --body='{"foo": "bar"}'

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for send-report


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	Organization ID (env: GF_ORG_ID)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgf-reports(1)\fP
